Nutrient Biology\nStem Cell Biology\nSystems Biology\nBiomedical Life Sciences\nThe Biomedical Life Sciences Program (BLS) is the umbrella PhD training program in biomedical sciences under VIBRE. The program was designed to spark scientific curiosity, give students a strong foundation in core biomedical knowledge, and provide the flexibility to shape their own training path. Students begin with shared coursework and research experiences that build broad skills, while also having the freedom to explore across disciplines and discover the research direction that best matches their interests both in the lab and in their future careers.\nWhile all students start with the same core foundation, the program also offers ten specialized tracks. This structure gives students the best of both worlds: a common intellectual framework that connects everyone, and the chance to dive deeply into advanced training within a specific discipline. Each track provides focused knowledge, techniques, and mentoring in its field, while still encouraging connections across the broader biomedical science programs.\nBiomedical Life Sciences Tracks\nThe Biomedical Life Sciences PhD tracks includes a core curriculum and focused training across ten tracks\nBiochemistry, Biophysics, and Structural Biology\nThe Biochemistry, Biophysics and Structural Biology PhD track applies physical principles and quantitative approaches to reveal how biomolecules fold, interact, and drive cellular physiology.\nBiochemistry, Biophysics, and Structural Biology\nCancer Biology\nThe Cancer Biology PhD Track investigates the molecular, genetic, and cellular mechanisms that drive tumor initiation and progression.\nCancer Biology\nCell and Molecular Biology\nThe Cell and Molecular Biology PhD track integrates pillar disciplines of biology to reveal how cells and their molecular components drive fundamental biological processes.\nCell and Molecular Biology\nComputational Biology\nThe Computational Life Sciences PhD track unites expertise from basic science and medicine to train students in developing and applying cutting-edge computational methods to complex challenges.\nComputational Biology\nDisease and Therapeutics\nThe Disease and Therapeutics PhD trains students to dissect the molecular and physiological mechanisms of disease and to develop innovative therapeutic solutions.\nDisease and Therapeutics\nGenetics\nThe Genetics PhD track investigates how genes and their regulation govern inheritance, variation, and disease, using approaches from classical genetics to modern genomics and epigenomics.\nGenetics\nImmunobiology and Microbial Sciences\nThe Immunobiology and Microbial Sciences PhD track integrates the study of the immune system with the biology of microbes to uncover how host\u2013pathogen interactions shape health and disease.\nImmunobiology and Microbial Sciences\nMetabolism and Nutrient Biology\nThe Metabolism and Nutrient Biology PhD track trains students to study metabolism from cells to organisms, linking basic science to therapies for obesity, diabetes, cancer, infections, and more.\nMetabolism and Nutrient Biology\nStem Cell Biology\nThe Stem Cell Biology PhD track trains students to study stem cells in development, repair, and regeneration, using tools like gene editing and bioengineering to advance research and therapies.\nStem Cell Biology\nSystems Biology\nThe Systems Biology track trains students to use data, computation, and AI to model complex biological networks, driving discoveries in basic science, therapy development, and personalized medicine.\nSystems Biology\nBack to top\nColumbia University Irving Medical Center\nNewYork-Presbyterian\nColumbiaDoctors\nAbout Us\nEducation\nResearch\nPatient Care\nInside VP&S\nFind People\nEvents\nAlumni\nCareers\nGive Now\nColumbia University Irving Medical Center\nVagelos College of Physicians & Surgeons\n630 West 168th Street\nNew York, NY 10032\nUnited States\nFollow Us\n\u00a9 2026 Columbia University\nPrivacy Po